Patch 001: surface whether index_share_for_mtp_iteration actually engages.

0xdfi/glm-5.2-dgx-spark-vllm027 findings.md flags this as an unconfirmed open
question: the QuantTrio checkpoint sets the flag in config.json, but engagement
depends on the draft model exposing set_skip_topk - and if the hook is missing
the sharing silently never happens. One boot with this patch answers it from
the serve log. No behavior change when the flag is false.

Applies to vllm v0.27.0 (vllm/v1/spec_decode/llm_base_proposer.py).
--- a/vllm/v1/spec_decode/llm_base_proposer.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/spec_decode/llm_base_proposer.py
@@ -1612,6 +1612,18 @@
             draft_hf_config, "index_share_for_mtp_iteration", False
         )
 
+        if self._share_mtp_indices:
+            _hook_owner = getattr(self.model, "model", None)
+            _hook_ok = hasattr(_hook_owner, "set_skip_topk")
+            logger.info(
+                "[glm52-collab] index_share_for_mtp_iteration=true resolved "
+                "from draft config (%s); set_skip_topk hook %s; indexer "
+                "sharing %s.",
+                getattr(draft_hf_config, "name_or_path", "unknown"),
+                "found" if _hook_ok else "MISSING",
+                "ENGAGED" if _hook_ok else
+                "will silently NOT engage (flag set, hook absent)",
+            )
         if self.use_local_argmax_reduction:
             if not hasattr(self.model, "get_top_tokens"):
                 raise ValueError(
